    "title": "Aerodynamic characteristics in pitch of the various wing-body configurations. (a) \u039b = 10.8\u00b0; t/c = 0.04.",
    "x_axis": "Lift coefficient, C_L, common to the three plots of the page and labelled only under the bottom (angle-of-attack) plot: -.2 at the left frame line, 0 at the heavy axis line, .8 at the right frame line, labels every 0.1. On the graph paper the heavy vertical lines fall every 0.05 C_L (about 69 px), a medium line halfway between them (every 0.025, about 34.6 px), fine lines every 0.005 (about 6.9 px). The C_L = 0 line is drawn heavier than the other heavy lines.",
    "y_axis": "Drag coefficient, C_D, scale on the right of the middle plot: labels 0, .04, .08, .12, .16, .20. The heavy horizontal lines fall every 0.02 C_D (about 68.5 px; the labels sit on every second one), a medium line halfway between them (every 0.01), fine lines every 0.002 (about 6.9 px). The C_D = 0 line is drawn heavier than the other heavy lines.",
    "content_note": "Middle plot of the page only (C_D against C_L). One faired curve with 8 hollow circles without a centre dot (radius about 13 px), all single: no doubled outline or second circle seen. Circle 2 (just left of C_L = 0) has the heavy 0.02 C_D line across its lower part and the faired curve through it; circle 3 has the heavy 0.10 C_L line running through it near its centre; circle 5 has its top edge on the heavy 0.06 C_D line and its right edge on the heavy 0.35 C_L line; circle 8 has its top edge on the heavy 0.18 C_D line and the heavy 0.70 C_L line through it. The scan shows 1-px steps in the grid lines along vertical seams (e.g. near x 605, 757 and 1822) and is slightly rotated (horizontal lines about 5 px lower at the right of the plot than at the left; vertical lines about 5 px further right at the top of the drag plot than at its bottom)."
  },
